 Pattern 4: Deque-Based Optimizations (Monotonic Deque)
The most high-powered Queue pattern. Keeps elements inside the Deque sorted in strictly monotonic order while allowing elements to be dropped from both ends in $O(1)$ time.
1. The Concept:
When finding maximums or minimums over dynamic ranges:
1. Remove from Tail (Back): Pop elements off the back if they are worse (e.g., smaller) than the incoming element, because they will never be selected again.
2. Remove from Head (Front): Pop the front element if its index falls outside the active sliding window boundary.

2. Java Blueprint (Sliding Window Maximum)

Java:

public int[] maxSlidingWindow(int[] nums, int k) {
    if (nums == null || nums.length == 0) return new int[0];
    
    int n = nums.length;
    int[] result = new int[n - k + 1];
    int resultIdx = 0;
    
    // Deque stores INDICES, not values
    Deque<Integer> deque = new ArrayDeque<>();
    
    for (int i = 0; i < nums.length; i++) {
        // 1. Out-of-bounds check: Remove elements at front if outside window [i - k + 1, i]
        if (!deque.isEmpty() && deque.peekFirst() < i - k + 1) {
            deque.pollFirst();
        }
        
        // 2. Maintain Monotonic Decreasing Order: Pop elements from back if smaller than nums[i]
        while (!deque.isEmpty() && nums[deque.peekLast()] < nums[i]) {
            deque.pollLast();
        }
        
        // 3. Add current index to back
        deque.offerLast(i);
        
        // 4. Record result once first window size 'k' is reached
        if (i >= k - 1) {
            result[resultIdx++] = nums[deque.peekFirst()]; // Maximum is always at the front!
        }
    }
    return result;
}

3. Essential Interview Questions
Hard: LeetCode 239 - Sliding Window Maximum (The exact template above)
Hard: LeetCode 862 - Shortest Subarray with Sum at Least K: Uses a Monotonic Deque combined with Prefix Sums. Maintains a monotonic increasing deque of prefix sums to find the shortest sub-segment matching the sum condition in $O(N)$ time.
Hard: LeetCode 1425 - Constrained Subsequence Sum: Dynamic Programming optimized by a Monotonic Deque.
Medium: LeetCode 1696 - Jump Game VI: DP transition $dp[i] = nums[i] + \max(dp[i-k \dots i-1])$ optimized using a Monotonic Deque to reduce time complexity from $O(N \cdot K)$ down to $O(N)$.
